pvr_alias: allow a dash in the display driver name

The alias is both the <name>_dri.so file and part of the
__driDriverGetExtensions_<name> symbol. The loader already maps '-' to '_'
when it looks the symbol up, so do the same for the define, otherwise a
display driver like sunxi-drm doesn't compile.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_alias/meson.build b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_alias/meson.build
index 128efd7..1d77004 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_alias/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_alias/meson.build
@@ -19,5 +19,5 @@
 # SOFTWARE.
 
 driver_pvr_alias = declare_dependency(
-  compile_args: '-DGALLIUM_PVR_ALIAS=@0@'.format(gallium_pvr_alias)
+  compile_args: '-DGALLIUM_PVR_ALIAS=@0@'.format(gallium_pvr_alias.replace('-', '_'))
 )
